## Dimension Design Instructions

### 1. Disclosure: {{ disclosure }}

Controls how much key information the patient reveals. Specify which item numbers are hidden and under what conditions they are revealed.

{% if disclosure == "responsive" %}
Answers what is asked without volunteering extra information. Pick 2-4 items the patient would mention on their own (chief complaint and most obvious associated symptoms); the rest are only shared when the doctor asks.
{% elif disclosure == "proactive" %}
Volunteers most information before being asked. Pick 1-2 items not volunteered (e.g., pertinent negatives); the rest are shared freely.
{% elif disclosure == "selective" %}
Shares selectively; things deemed unimportant or embarrassing are omitted. Pick 3-5 items hidden; shared only when the doctor asks about the relevant topic.
{% elif disclosure == "reluctant" %}
Reluctant to share; needs repeated questioning. Pick 5-8 items hidden; deflects on first ask, reveals on follow-up.
{% elif disclosure == "withholding" %}
Deliberately hides information; denies even when asked directly. Pick 8-11 items hidden; only admits after persistent questioning and trust-building.
{% endif %}

**Principles:** Hidden items should be clinically significant; hiding motivation must be realistic (embarrassment, fear, perceived irrelevance); don't hide the chief complaint; item 0 (demographics) is typically not hidden. Hidden lists grow with each level.

### 2. Cognition: {{ cognition }}

Patient's understanding of their illness/symptoms. Provide specific phrases the patient would say.

{% if cognition == "accurate" %}
Correctly understands their symptoms; describes them objectively without exaggeration or minimization; does not guess at a diagnosis. Provide 2-3 specific, accurate statements the patient would say.
{% elif cognition == "partial_understanding" %}
Roughly knows something is wrong but unclear on details. E.g., "I think it might be XX, but I'm not sure."
{% elif cognition == "misconception" %}
Has a specific wrong attribution (e.g., "just stress", "caught a cold") and firmly believes it.
{% elif cognition == "web_self_diagnosis" %}
Looked up symptoms online and has a specific incorrect self-diagnosis they repeatedly mention. Should be plausible but wrong.
{% elif cognition == "folk_remedy" %}
Believes in folk remedies/herbal treatments; has tried or plans to use a specific remedy. Skeptical of modern medicine.
{% elif cognition == "complete_denial" %}
Denies any problem; came because family/friends insisted. Repeatedly says "I'm sure it's nothing."
{% endif %}

**Principles:** Content must relate to this case; self-diagnosis should pick a different disease with similar symptoms; folk remedies should be culturally realistic.

### 3. Logic: {{ logic }}

{% if logic == "consistent" %}
Patient's narrative is fully consistent with no contradictions. Provide 2-3 key points the patient would describe consistently every time (timing, severity, details, etc.).

**Principles:** Key points should cover core facts about symptoms (timing, severity, triggers, etc.) and remain consistent in wording across the conversation.
{% else %}
Design contradictions in the patient's narrative.

{% if logic == "minor_inconsistency" %}
1-2 small discrepancies (e.g., "about two days" vs "maybe three days") that don't affect the overall picture.
{% elif logic == "occasional_contradiction" %}
2-3 contradictions involving symptom presence/timing/severity. Corrects when pointed out.
{% elif logic == "frequent_contradiction" %}
3-4 contradictions, including denying previous statements. Won't self-correct.
{% elif logic == "fabricating" %}
2-3 fabricated symptoms or denials of real ones. Plausible but inconsistent with actual history.
{% endif %}

**Principles:** Contradictions based on real information; vary types (temporal/existential/severity); fabrications must be plausible.
{% endif %}

### 4. Attitude: {{ attitude }}

Design the patient's consultation attitude. Provide case-specific phrases and behaviors.

{% if attitude == "compliant" %}
Fully cooperative, answers willingly, friendly, trusts the doctor. Provide 2-3 cooperative phrases (e.g., proactively asking about tests needed, expressing willingness to follow advice).
{% elif attitude == "reluctant" %}
Reserved, gives short answers, needs doctor to draw out details. Provide 2-3 scenarios and phrases.
{% elif attitude == "impatient" %}
Wants to finish quickly, annoyed by detailed questioning. Provide the reason and 2-3 impatient phrases.
{% elif attitude == "evasive" %}
Deflects when asked about sensitive topics. Specify what they avoid and why.
{% elif attitude == "resistant" %}
Refuses to cooperate with certain questions or examinations. Specify what and why.
{% elif attitude == "dominant" %}
Tries to control the conversation, tells the doctor what to do. Specify what they demand.
{% endif %}

**Principles:** Motivation must be realistic (fear/cost/time pressure/past experience); behavior must relate to the case.

### 5. Purpose: {{ purpose }}

Design the patient's real reason for visiting.

{% if purpose == "symptom_relief" %}
Wants symptom relief — symptoms are affecting daily life. Describe specifically how symptoms impact daily life, provide 2-3 related phrases.
{% elif purpose == "reassurance" %}
Wants to confirm nothing serious is wrong. Specify what disease they fear and why (family history, read online, etc.).
{% elif purpose == "medication_request" %}
Wants a specific medication. Specify the drug name/type and reason (used before, friend recommended, etc.).
{% endif %}

**Principles:** Content must relate to the case; reassurance needs specific fears; medication_request needs specific drug names.

### 6. Expression: {{ expression }}

Design the patient's communication style. Provide specific example phrases.

{% if expression == "clear" %}
Organized and precise; uses timeline or prioritizes key symptoms naturally. Provide 2-3 well-structured statements.
{% elif expression == "normal" %}
Everyday language; gets the point across but isn't very organized; the doctor may need to follow up for details. Provide 2-3 typical everyday expressions.
{% elif expression == "vague" %}
Imprecise wording, unclear symptom descriptions. Provide 2-3 vague statements.
{% elif expression == "verbose" %}
Repetitive, adds unnecessary details. Provide 2-3 topics the patient over-elaborates on.
{% elif expression == "tangential" %}
Frequently goes off-topic. {% if social_history %}Based on social background, design 2-3 topics they ramble about.{% else %}Based on the patient's age, occupation, and other demographics, design 2-3 topics they ramble about.{% endif %}
{% elif expression == "incoherent" %}
Jumps between topics, mixes up timelines, confuses cause and effect. Provide 2-3 examples.
{% endif %}

**Principles:** Style should match the patient's background; provide specific example phrases.

